    "updated_at": "2026-09-24T19:28:30Z",
    "body": "> Chromium fails the subtest `Sandboxed iframe with allow-top-navigation can close top window` in https://wpt.fyi/results/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-iframe-element/sandbox-top-close.sub.window.html , does this need a bug to be filed?\r\n\r\nOh, I had completely missed that, thanks! I actually had tested that case (my original test was UI based, not WPT based), and chromium seemed to work fine. I didn't look at the WPT result for all browsers till just then since it matched my test. Turns out what is happening is that chromium is indeed closing the window, and this is a timing issue where \"is closing\" isn't seen immediately by the opener at the point, so javascript doesn't immediately observe \"is closing\".\r\n\r\nissue reported now!",
